61a60dbc>On this page</div><ul class="VPDocOutlineItem root" data-v-61a60dbc data-v-e88eb560><!--[--><!--]--></ul></div></nav><!--[--><!--]--><div class="spacer" data-v-f129a94b></div><!--[--><!--]--><!----><!--[--><!--]--><!--[--><!--]--></div></div></div></div><div class="content" data-v-fd2f0f74><div class="content-container" data-v-fd2f0f74><!--[--><!--[--><!--[--><div class="doc-actions"><nav class="doc-actions__breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/libraries/sdk">Libraries</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">For AI agents</span></nav><button type="button"><svg class="doc-actions__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="8" y="8" width="11" height="11" rx="2"></rect><path d="M16 8V6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v8a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h2"></path></svg> Copy page link</button><span class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite"></span></div><!--]--><!--]--><!--]--><main class="main" data-v-fd2f0f74><div style="position:relative;" class="vp-doc _libraries_for-agents" data-v-fd2f0f74><div><h1 id="for-ai-agents" tabindex="-1">For AI agents <a class="header-anchor" href="#for-ai-agents" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;For AI agents&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Use <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> to find the Markdown reference for your task. Read <a href="https://docs.voicelab.uz/AGENTS.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">AGENTS.md</a> for credentials, retries, and tool safety. These files are public and need no API key or JavaScript.</p><p>For several APIs at once, fetch <a href="/llms-api.txt">llms-api.txt</a>. For one API, fetch its page, such as <a href="https://docs.voicelab.uz/markdown/api/tts.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">TTS Markdown</a>.</p><h2 id="context-fetching-protocol" tabindex="-1">Context Fetching Protocol <a class="header-anchor" href="#context-fetching-protocol" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Context Fetching Protocol&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>Fetch <code>https://docs.voicelab.uz/llms.txt</code> and select the relevant reference.</li><li>Read the current request fields, authentication, responses, and limits before coding.</li><li>If the docs are unavailable or conflict with the response, report what you could not verify. Do not invent routes or copy another provider&#39;s contract.</li></ol><p>Add these links to your agent&#39;s configuration. Publishing <code>AGENTS.md</code> alone neither configures external agents nor grants account permissions.</p><h2 id="environment" tabindex="-1">Environment <a class="header-anchor" href="#environment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Environment&quot;">​</a></h2><div class="language-bash vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">bash</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-dark github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#F97583;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">export</span><span style="--shiki-light:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> VOICELAB_API_KEY</span><span style="--shiki-light:#F97583;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">vlk_your_secret</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Keep this secret in the tool runtime, never in a model prompt or browser bundle. Product endpoints authenticate with <code>Authorization: Bearer $VOICELAB_API_KEY</code>. Account-management endpoints require a user access JWT instead.</p><h2 id="recommended-agent-flow" tabindex="-1">Recommended agent flow <a class="header-anchor" href="#recommended-agent-flow" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Recommended agent flow&quot;">​</a></h2><p>For TTS:</p><ol><li>Call <code>GET /v1/tts/languages</code>.</li><li>Call <code>GET /v1/voices?language={code}</code>.</li><li>Call <code>POST /v1/tts</code> with a unique idempotency key.</li><li>Save <code>200</code> WAV audio. For <code>202</code>, poll <code>GET /v1/tts/generations/{id}</code> until <code>completed</code> or <code>failed</code>; then download <code>audio_url</code> without API credentials.</li></ol><p>For STT:</p><ol><li>Call <code>POST /v1/stt</code> with multipart audio and a UUID idempotency key.</li><li>Save the <code>202</code> response&#39;s ID. Poll <code>GET /v1/stt/transcriptions/{id}</code> with <code>stt:read</code> until <code>completed</code> or <code>failed</code>. Read <code>transcript</code> only on completion. Resume the same ID after a timeout.</li><li>Use the history, editor, or export endpoints when the task requires durable output.</li></ol><p>For <a href="/api/voice-isolator">Voice Isolator</a>:</p><ol><li>Use a key with <code>audio_isolation</code> Access.</li><li>Submit multipart <code>file</code> to <code>POST /v1/voice-isolations</code> with a UUID idempotency key. Reuse that key and content on retries.</li><li>Poll job detail, including MP3 preparation after inference completes. Stop on a failed job or failed audio conversion.</li><li>Download <code>audio_url</code> without forwarding the API key. Refresh detail when a signed URL expires.</li><li>Request an export only if a different format is needed. DELETE hides history and does not cancel processing or erase audio.</li></ol><p>For <a href="/api/llm">LLM</a>:</p><ol><li>Use a key with <code>llm</code> Access and read <code>GET /v1/models</code> for IDs, prices, and limits.</li><li>Send <code>POST /v1/chat/completions</code> with caller-supplied messages and a unique idempotency key.</li><li>For SSE, parse events and wait for <code>[DONE]</code>; HTTP <code>200</code> alone is insufficient.</li><li>Capture <code>X-LLM-Request-ID</code> and inspect <code>GET /v1/llm/requests/{id}</code> after an interrupted response or duplicate retry.</li><li>Execute validated function calls in your application. Submit tool results in a new paid completion with a new idempotency key.</li><li>Contact support for <code>llm_model_temporarily_unavailable</code> or <code>llm_usage_pending</code>. These holds require reconciliation; waiting or changing keys does not clear them. An upstream <code>499</code> does not prove zero cost.</li></ol><p>For browser realtime work, your backend calls <code>POST /v1/ticket</code> with required <code>transport=websocket</code> and <code>service=tts</code> or <code>stt</code>. Success is <code>201 Created</code>. Use the short-lived ticket only on the matching service. Both services also accept server-side <code>xvl-api-key</code> on the handshake, but never send it together with a ticket. Never place the API key itself in a WebSocket URL.</p><h2 id="tool-definitions" tabindex="-1">Tool definitions <a class="header-anchor" href="#tool-definitions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tool definitions&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Resolve <code>voice_id</code> from the voice catalog before calling the TTS tool.</p><div class="language-json vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">json</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-dark github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#E1E4E8;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">[</span></span>
